{"title":"2022 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 24","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Absolute_Values_and_Inequalities)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Absolute Values and Inequalities)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Lipschitz_Condition)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Lipschitz Condition)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Slopes)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Slopes)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Translation)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Translation)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_Using_Algebraic_Manipulation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn Using Algebraic Manipulation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider functions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" /> that satisfy <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/7/807767b613ba502ffb8480dcb6ec61bc4f0f8fd2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|f(x)-f(y)|\\leq \\frac{1}{2}|x-y|\\]\" width=\"188\" height=\"37\" /> for all real numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />. Of all such functions that also satisfy the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/72850fce128cf8a7ee67a58c0ee202cf6906735b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(300) = f(900)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />, what is the greatest possible value of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/0/dc03e872a46ec49f679240b312b43547ea012bd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[f(f(800))-f(f(400))?\\]\" width=\"183\" height=\"18\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/1/cd1002108a40dbef99e42321023a63e488ee2d64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 25 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)}\\ 100 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)}\\ 150 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)}\\ 200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"424\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Absolute_Values_and_Inequalities.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Absolute_Values_and_Inequalities)\">Solution 1 (Absolute Values and Inequalities)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Absolute Values and Inequalities)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/c/9bc851cfd276960a508dcb5174fdaaaf1e923521.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |f(f(800))-f(f(400))| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|f(800)-f(400)| &amp;&amp;(\\bigstar) \\\\ &amp;\\leq \\frac12\\left|\\frac12|800-400|\\right| \\\\ &amp;= 100, \\end{align*}\" width=\"417\" height=\"110\" />\nfrom which we eliminate answer choices <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/3/0/b305929a95b53f14a0ad53eba1d8560626e1f28b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(D)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/2/5729ea372cb53da5f2596d6f802dbd34914d4322.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(E)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"31\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Note that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/7/f/27f337842a4744654a78fe0d8dedac64c079ac38.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{8} |f(800)-f(300)| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|800-300| &amp;&amp;= 250, \\\\ |f(800)-f(900)| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|800-900| &amp;&amp;= 50, \\\\ |f(400)-f(300)| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|400-300| &amp;&amp;= 50, \\\\ |f(400)-f(900)| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|400-900| &amp;&amp;= 250. \\\\ \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"314\" height=\"166\" />\nLet <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/9/4/6940d26d07ffda05f960290dc50139cc5ac6964d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a=f(300)=f(900).$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" /> Together, it follows that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/3/da37d7cdb5ec2180c9e6ee3ebfb5d82df9567592.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |f(800)-a|&amp;\\leq 50, \\\\ |f(400)-a|&amp;\\leq 50. \\\\ \\end{align*}\" width=\"138\" height=\"43\" />\nWe rewrite <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/7/5/875816dba06e32edf79fcfbb793af13f73bdca9c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\bigstar)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"29\" height=\"18\" /> as\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/a/aba9fe3374273b6068b6dd5411e514d95786de01.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} |f(f(800))-f(f(400))| &amp;\\leq \\frac12|f(800)-f(400)| \\\\ &amp;= \\frac12|(f(800)-a)-(f(400)-a)| \\\\ &amp;\\leq \\frac12|50-(-50)| \\\\ &amp;=\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50}. \\end{align*}\" width=\"448\" height=\"158\" />\n~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Lipschitz_Condition.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Lipschitz_Condition)\">Solution 2 (Lipschitz Condition)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Lipschitz Condition)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Denote <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/d/16db787f880469a46246ec2a7a3f34aaa0c67ef1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(900)-f(600) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />.\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/8/72850fce128cf8a7ee67a58c0ee202cf6906735b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(300) = f(900)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"131\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/0/7/b07c2658f6dbbf53c1bf833f72aaa7c5c2324d92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(300) - f(600) = a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"162\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>Following from the Lipschitz condition given in this problem, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/6/d/76da46b95b957573db5b23d9cc8575d88459bc26.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|a| \\leq 150$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" /> and\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/8/918800841c78f42f0e9566a02ee3dedced1c9412.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ f(800) - f(600) \\leq \\min \\left\\{ a + 50 , 100 \\right\\} \\]\" width=\"286\" height=\"18\" />\nand\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/d/c/6dcd4c3e6148f2f2d6d69ae7d90769fd0f711ef3.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ f(400) - f(600) \\geq \\max \\left\\{ a - 50 , -100 \\right\\} . \\]\" width=\"311\" height=\"18\" />\nThus,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/f/f3fdd29d9ef77a16b20b75e6ee40d9f79edd3634.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(800) - f(400) &amp; \\leq \\min \\left\\{ a + 50 , 100 \\right\\} - \\max \\left\\{ a - 50 , -100 \\right\\}  \\\\ &amp; = 100 + \\min \\left\\{ a, 50 \\right\\} - \\max \\left\\{ a , - 50 \\right\\} \\\\ &amp; = 100 + \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} a + 50 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\leq -50 \\\\ 0 &amp; \\mbox{ if } -50 &lt; a &lt; 50 \\\\ -a + 50 &amp; \\mbox{ if } a \\geq 50 \\end{array} \\right. . \\end{align*}\" width=\"463\" height=\"114\" />\nThus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aeac8aa6bcbe962747a91a5acd61e928a9ba2a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800) - f(400)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> is maximized at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/2/6/726822ca0bf66b33200c0773824573df23bd134f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800)-f(600) = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/2/cc234ab6b3e3e693f30bb5622f05e3e160e91dc3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(400)-f(600)=-50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />, with the maximal value 100.\n</p><p>By symmetry, following from an analogous argument, we can show that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/a/aeac8aa6bcbe962747a91a5acd61e928a9ba2a6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800) - f(400)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"129\" height=\"20\" /> is minimized at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/9/b5969c2cfb1ffadf981fbbddcf796c8eb0037546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 0$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/4/084c062056d65182fbb9292b824703365838318c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800)-f(600) = -50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"185\" height=\"20\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c5e43bd650409779bfdb418ce77eb416320f2a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(400)-f(600)=50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"171\" height=\"20\" />, with the minimal value <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/0/060d8850e65d5781ce12d9fe2681f401dd6ee77c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"40\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Following from the Lipschitz condition,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/7/0e7aa23688fba18784e35397668d7daf4589dd62.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{align*} f(f(800)) - f(f(400)) &amp; \\leq \\frac{1}{2} \\left| f(800) - f(400) \\right| \\\\ &amp; \\leq 50 . \\end{align*}\" width=\"351\" height=\"60\" />\nWe have already construct instances in which the second inequality above is augmented to an equality.\n</p><p>Now, we construct an instance in which the first inequality above is augmented to an equality.\n</p><p>Consider the following piecewise-linear function:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/2/8/9280b948ea59469e86f27717d3836bb58ed9d3b8.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[ f(x) = \\left\\{ \\begin{array}{ll} \\frac{1}{2} \\left( x - 300 \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } x \\leq 300 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\left( x - 300 \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } 300 &lt; x \\leq 400 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} \\left( x - 600 \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } 400 &lt; x \\leq 800 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} \\left( x - 900 \\right) &amp; \\mbox{ if } x &gt; 800 \\end{array} \\right.. \\]\" width=\"352\" height=\"85\" />\nTherefore, the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/2/e222d9c2df15ba10624515462133c165335939ef.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(f(800)) - f(f(400))$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"179\" height=\"20\" /> is\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/6/d569c17de09425fa2ff3d9bd3df9e9e8abf0d2ab.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"65\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p><p>~Viliciri (LaTeX edits)\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Slopes.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Slopes)\">Solution 3 (Slopes)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Slopes)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Divide both sides by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/0/6c0a86663edb0dccee099a47d48b1b19a4ee6cb9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x - y|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> to get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/81381fb4decddc4751b4cce81e2a371bf674f1d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{|f(x) - f(y)|}{|x - y|} \\leq \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -18px\" width=\"145\" height=\"45\" />. This means that when we take any two points on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/b/2/bb2c93730dbb48558bb3c4738c956c4e8f816437.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"13\" height=\"18\" />, the absolute value of the slope between the two points is at most <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/4/7c4966b18c779d400eb58eaebed2c4b531029983.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(300) = f(900) = c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"163\" height=\"20\" />, and since we want to find the maximum value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/1/b716a442757edd848ba740f2b2972c702e7b51d8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(800) - f(400)|$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"139\" height=\"20\" />, we can take the most extreme case and draw a line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/7/7/a7748d3d38355a68b51bddc29d7647230728287e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$-\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"29\" height=\"38\" /> down from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/e/a1e07bebd6695d6c5a79d6653d06d84b10bb36be.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(300)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8571f6a0a320c319eca26765b247c6970b973ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(400)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> and a line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" /> up from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65974491c33ce619afc13049cd8781cd15c2bee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/9/5/395ce2436ffc43d263f05a15f3951c35b1971d39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(900)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/7/cd74ac80217c9939f7c234df98092fc06e7ac162.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(400) = c - 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/f/5/3f5caaa70c36277ade39a2ee35359eab94c56ce1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800) = c + 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"127\" height=\"20\" />, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/4/bf4f0615a605173f7882a8d90d5f7eb9084edf8e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(800) - f(400)| = |c + 50 - (c - 50)| = 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"357\" height=\"20\" />, and this is attainable because the slope of the line connecting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/5/a8571f6a0a320c319eca26765b247c6970b973ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(400)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"54\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/65974491c33ce619afc13049cd8781cd15c2bee6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$f(800)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" /> still has absolute value less than <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/9/2f960094315d60883495f9b74148e17487ee9584.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"15\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3bacd4b2c71660be9a471969b5f56da7526577c8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|f(f(800)) - f(f(400))| \\leq \\frac{1}{2}|f(800) - f(400)| = \\frac{1}{2}(100) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"529\" height=\"38\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Translation.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Translation)\">Solution 4 (Translation)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Translation)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/f/c8f3d1eb368e10acd95a219c872535b171e15fad.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x) = f(x)-f(300)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"170\" height=\"20\" />. Then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/9/659a6a2610357101d77dbae8eb9bf0b3100c08fd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"32\" height=\"18\" /> satisfies all the conditions and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/d/aeda77cc2c3a05d97187967e82330accfb052423.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(300) = g(900) = 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"161\" height=\"20\" />. We would want <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/a/6bae940cb834870d4af1ff30c615a2de5d3e8dbb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(400)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79ce1266d1477e11f10ab21c2437b10c15cadca1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(800)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"53\" height=\"20\" /> as distant from each other as possible. So assign <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/f/99f374881ed04935d20c3ed3d789115341016c68.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(400) = -50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"109\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/7/267ed064af31b36a4822656baa7715eef2bbd445.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$g(800) = 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"95\" height=\"20\" />, the possible lower and upper bounds respectively. It follows that one can obtain the upper bound for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/e/c0e7bf1e92b9f280319222e6e0d68b7316585ae5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|g(g(800)) - g(g(400))| = |g(50) - g(-50  )| \\leq \\frac{1}{2}(100) = \\boxed{\\textbf{(B)}\\ 50}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"503\" height=\"38\" /> as the answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/2Li0IYOQCFQ\">https://youtu.be/2Li0IYOQCFQ</a>\n</p><p>~Steven Chen (Professor Chen Education Palace, www.professorchenedu.com)\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_Using_Algebraic_Manipulation\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn Using Algebraic Manipulation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn Using Algebraic Manipulation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/-yzpw6b3_KA\">https://youtu.be/-yzpw6b3_KA</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2022_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_24&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/n0ZTR6edOBs\">https://youtu.be/n0ZTR6edOBs</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-brac